@startuml AD-003-task-estimation-ml-pipeline
!theme plain
title Effort & cost estimation (UC-024) - Activity Diagram
' Rewritten 2026-10-26 (Phase 6, Task 25) to match the implementation: a per-role regression
' learnt from finished projects instead of an embedding search + gradient boosting pipeline.

|System|
start
:workflow.started (EstimationHandler);
:TrainingDataCollector:\none sample per finished project and role\n(features: description length, use case count;\n targets: agent time, LLM cost);
if (Model cached for this history?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :EstimationModel.train();
  while (for each agent role)
    if (samples >= 6?) then (yes)
      :RegressionEstimator\n(ridge least squares, floor = smallest value seen);
    else (no)
      :MedianEstimator;
    endif
    :Leave-one-out error (MAPE / MAE);
  endwhile
endif
if (Any finished project?) then (yes)
  :Forecast per role, sum for the project,\nconfidence low / medium / high;
  :Store ProjectEstimate (stage = start);
else (no)
  :No forecast (tasks keep estimatedCost = null);
  stop
endif

|PM Agent|
:Break the plan into tasks;

|System|
:Store ProjectEstimate (stage = planned);
:estimateTaskCost = (DEV + QC + QA cost) / task count;
:Create tasks with estimatedCost (AgentTaskStrategy);

|Board Member|
:Open Reports > Effort & cost forecast\n(GET /projects/:id/estimate);
if (Project finished?) then (yes)
  :See the start forecast against the outcome\n(compareForecast);
endif
stop
@enduml
